# What never belongs in the build context (t250).
#
# Mirrors `.gitignore`, with the same reasoning: everything here is either
# reproduced inside the image (`npm ci` rebuilds `node_modules` for the image's
# own platform, and a macOS `better-sqlite3` copied in would be worse than
# useless) or is local state that has nothing to do with a build. Keeping the
# context small is the cheap part; keeping a developer's database and history
# out of a published image is the point.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in the build, at any depth
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# History and CI: the image is built from the tree, not from the repository
.git
.gitignore
.github/

# Local state of the control plane (D1) — the operator's database, and any
# credential hash inside it
.cartografo/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Build artefacts and tool caches
dist/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# Working notes and the ticket tool's cached profile
notes/
.flowpilot/

# System
.DS_Store

# The container artefacts themselves: changing a comment here should not
# invalidate the `COPY . .` layer
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
compose.yml
